# TRANSOVO UX GOVERNANCE — MANDATORY (ALWAYS)

The files in `docs/TRANSOVO-*.md` (excluding Kimi orchestration docs) are **HARD REQUIREMENTS**, not optional design inspiration. They are enforced via `.cursor/rules/transovo-*.mdc`.

## You MUST

1. Treat every Transovo UX/design standard as a **binding implementation rule**.
2. Read `docs/TRANSOVO-PRODUCT-DESIGN-UX-GOVERNANCE.md` before UI, IA, layout, visual, or interaction changes.
3. Read **every applicable** standards guide for the surface you touch (accessibility, forms, tables, etc.).
4. Follow **authority order** when documents conflict — governance wins over visual polish; scope wins over convenience.
5. Fix **shared systems** (tokens, components, shell) instead of page-specific patches.
6. Ensure visible controls reflect **actual runtime truth** — no fake states, no dead toggles.

## You MUST NOT

- Design pages independently without the standards system.
- Invent features, nav homes, or terminology outside approved product scope.
- Use arbitrary colors, spacing, typography, or one-off components when shared system exists.
- Ship UI that violates WCAG 2.2 AA, keyboard/focus rules, form validation rules, or privacy/consent UX.
- Treat `docs/TRANSOVO-*` as "nice to have" reference material.

